      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Pain is a rarely acknowledged complication of chronic wounds, yet for those who live with it, it is often the over-riding preoccupation. In this article, the author--who herself has suffered for many years with wound pain--discusses why pain is not widely acknowledged by health professionals caring for wounds, and highlights why awareness of it is central to holistic care."},
